d the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\: \\cos t, \\: t \\rangle$\nfrom  $t =0$ to $t = 2\\pi.$" 13194139536157 false] [17592186119599 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/8573aedcd26cba038b2db072560cd3d6ba7676542888a2d9b8a356713eaf6724.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\: \\cos t, \\: t \\rangle$\nfrom  $t =0$ to $t = 2\\pi.$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186119667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386490 13194139536157 true] [17592186119667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386497 13194139536157 true] [17592186119667 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386504 13194139536157 true] [17592186119668 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386469 13194139536157 true] [17592186119668 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386476 13194139536157 true] [17592186119668 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386511 13194139536157 true] [17592186119781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386483 13194139536157 true] [17592186120455 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536157 true] [17592186120455 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536157 false] [17592186120455 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/9b83db0bb11b8e4bbcc4b04b7bf696879d4d7f4732d6aef7d005f9da2b625526.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨2{t}^{3/2},\\,3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=3.$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186120455 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1837/Source/Images/q-77066.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g} ( t ) = \\langle  2 {t}^{3 / 2} , \\, 3 t \\rangle$ from $t = 0$ to $t = 3$." 13194139536157 false] [17592186120455 1145 "Differentiate: $\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle3\\sqrt t,3\\rangle$, so the speed is $3\\sqrt{t+1}$. Therefore $$L=\\int_0^3 3\\sqrt{t+1}\\,dt=[2(t+1)^{3/2}]_0^3=2(8-1)=14.$$" 13194139536157 false] [17592186120455 1145 "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\sqrt{t},\\,3⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{t})^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9t+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3(t+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2(t+1)^{3/2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =16-2 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186330106 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052793/assets/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$" 13194139536157 false] [17592186330106 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386469 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386470 13194139536157 true] [17592186386469 1089 "q-127585" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386469 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536157 true] [17592186386469 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/c4aa91668440687bbae4b1f85672f5cbaf7ce00d978049c7558eed99b7361d1a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨3t-{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=1.$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386469 1113 #uuid "1c41e24c-0b02-5456-808b-29702e52055c" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386469 1145 "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3-3{t}^{2},\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(3-3{t}^{2})}^{2}+{(6t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9-18{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =3({t}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+1-[\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+(-1)]) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}+1+\\frac{1}{3}+1) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386471 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386472 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386473 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386474 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386475 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1041 "selection" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386472 13194139536157 true] [17592186386470 1110 #uuid "94a3a2fb-5a98-5825-9cf3-61f79671bb47" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386471 1034 "4\\sqrt{2}" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386471 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386471 1111 #uuid "eaea0aa4-af5f-5e60-a200-0b26c23c53da" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386472 1034 "8" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386472 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386472 1111 #uuid "6856beae-0384-5fdb-a24b-5364f9fe57b4" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386473 1034 "6" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386473 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386473 1111 #uuid "f39aca7e-a3c8-560b-806c-bdc701f9ec5a" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386474 1034 "4" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386474 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386474 1111 #uuid "6148606a-b419-5da4-8087-5071562d478e" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386475 1034 "3\\sqrt{2}" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386475 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386475 1111 #uuid "01ed9fa1-c8dc-5157-aeec-4aca75494731" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386476 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386477 13194139536157 true] [17592186386476 1089 "q-127602" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386476 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536157 true] [17592186386476 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081725/assets/33412629fc30584cf4a1726eef7e4f23f623ae4439d25045d61e36f68914dacd.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{3}({t}^{2}+2)^{3/2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=2.$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386476 1113 #uuid "1df62e56-e883-5fdf-91e4-8c4a1c360268" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386476 1145 "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}({t}^{2}+2)^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}({t}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}({t}^{2}+1)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t){|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+2)-(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}+2+\\frac{1}{3}+1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386478 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386479 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386480 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386481 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386482 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1041 "selection" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386481 13194139536157 true] [17592186386477 1110 #uuid "8b2cd560-6ea1-5b15-9bd9-294d986283a1" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386478 1034 "\\frac{16}{3}" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386478 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386478 1111 #uuid "1d0c1590-cb77-5ed1-b4b4-6f68391f9bb9" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386479 1034 "8" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386479 1111 #uuid "0ffaed98-5e50-502a-822a-dbab396427fc" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386480 1034 "\\frac{11}{3}" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386480 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386480 1111 #uuid "3c865a2d-09e5-5d3b-80e0-3a504ff4e99e" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386481 1034 "6" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386481 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386481 1111 #uuid "10495939-2abf-5cdc-bb93-cfa02699e239" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386482 1034 "4" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386482 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386482 1111 #uuid "9267559c-62da-5abb-916c-0ff5c6123751" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386483 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386484 13194139536157 true] [17592186386483 1089 "q-127635" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386483 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536157 true] [17592186386483 1100 "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=0.$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386483 1113 #uuid "296a9cc9-0f93-53af-89f8-f5d81544c725" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386483 1145 "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{({t}^{2})}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+2)^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({t}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+2t){|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}+2(0))-(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+2(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386485 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386486 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386487 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386488 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386489 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1041 "selection" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386489 13194139536157 true] [17592186386484 1110 #uuid "2b70033d-cb5e-5200-9f2e-7c95f5566b55" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386485 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386485 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386485 1111 #uuid "cce2d06a-3857-5e4a-82c9-78255952db4d" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386486 1034 "\\frac{11}{6}" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386486 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386486 1111 #uuid "09ed347c-cf90-5b69-b821-4c6eb7883f8a" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386487 1034 "3" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386487 1111 #uuid "ecda2a41-0dd7-51fc-ac8d-3bd95987cae0" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386488 1034 "4" 13194139536157 true] [17592186386488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536157 true] [17592186386488 1111 #uuid "810d1fe2-54f0-5011-bbd6-504ad832ee01" 1319